1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,543
Make OpenBEXI Discovery your own. Start in the installed local app, then create a profile
for your research.

2
00:00:07,543 --> 00:00:16,013
Choose Connect AI. Select your provider, paste your API key, and save. OpenAI is the
default.

3
00:00:16,013 --> 00:00:22,327
The key step is Create new profile. Open Settings, then choose the button at the top.

4
00:00:22,327 --> 00:00:31,991
Describe your field or area of interest, not just a title. For example: understand dark
matter, dark energy, and the expanding universe.

5
00:00:31,991 --> 00:00:40,624
Choose a reasoning level from Medium to Ultra. Higher levels may take longer and use more
tokens. Then create your profile.

6
00:00:40,624 --> 00:00:48,152
AI chooses a name and builds your overview, goals, and topics. This demonstration uses an
example response.

7
00:00:48,152 --> 00:00:55,520
Review the orange AI-generated overview and the topic checkboxes. Your new profile opens
its own workspace.

8
00:00:55,520 --> 00:01:05,921
Write a question. Overall Search is broad. Specific Search focuses on checked topics or
sources. For web search, use OpenAI.

9
00:01:05,921 --> 00:01:12,575
Switch profiles in Settings. Your selected profile returns when you reopen the local app.

10
00:01:12,575 --> 00:01:21,308
Always open the sources and verify the results. Start with a clear field. Create your
profile. Then explore.
